# Commit and push

- **Every time** you change code, commit and push before you stop. No exceptions. Do not ask whether to commit or push.
- If the user says "push this" or similar, push immediately — even if you think it was already pushed; run `git push origin HEAD:main` and report the result.
- After finishing any task (bug fix, feature, config), create a git commit and push in the same turn. Never leave unpushed commits on `master`.
- Push with `git push origin HEAD:main` (local `master` tracks `origin/main`). Do not force-push.
- PowerShell: pass the commit message with a here-string, not bash HEREDOC.
- Do not skip hooks. Do not update git config.
- Contact lookup is for reaching the current homeowner of the pinned house (public listing / assessor-style sources). Do not skip-trace personal Google/Facebook accounts, profile photos, or people-search pages of former residents.
